findings.fix:
Remove the manual replace and let `JSON.stringify` handle escaping:
```tsx
const baseUrl = process.env.OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL ?? "https://omnibridge-dev.vercel.app/api/v1";
...
<script
  dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{
    __html: `window.__OMNIBRIDGE_BASE_URL__ = ${JSON.stringify(baseUrl)};`
  }}
/>
```

Prefix the paths with a leading slash and ensure they are handled by server‑side middleware that enforces authentication:
```ts
export default [
  // ...
  route("/api/v1/chat/completions", "routes/api.v1.chat.completions.ts"),
  route("/api/v1/models", "routes/api.v1.models.ts"),
  // ...
] satisfies RouteConfig;
```

Guard the import with a dynamic `import()` that falls back to a no‑op handler when the build does not exist, or adjust the start script to always run after a successful build. Example fix:
```js
let build = {};
try {
  build = await import("../build/server/index.js");
} catch (e) {
  console.warn("Build not found, running in dev mode – request handler will be a placeholder.");
}
export default createRequestHandler({ build });
```
